  "interpretation": {
    "original_model_interpretation": "This synthetic GENE1 allele is rendered to exercise the complete report pathway. The retained gene-disease record provides contextual support for a synthetic neurodevelopmental condition with autosomal dominant inheritance, but it does not establish that this allele is causal. The allele is rare in the primary population dataset, was not identified in the retained 1000 Genomes exact query, and has a source-preserving fallback population observation.\n\nNCBI ClinVar reports an uncertain-significance classification with single-submitter review context. GeneBe supplies an automated uncertain-significance annotation; this remains attributed automated evidence and is not adopted as an application classification. SIFT, PolyPhen-2, and CADD results provide concordant computational concern, but computational predictions do not independently establish pathogenicity.\n\nThe accepted phenotype is partially supported: one synthetic neurologic feature overlaps retained gene context, while the remaining feature is not established by the available evidence. The literature entries describe general interpretation standards and are not allele-specific proof. No material classification conflict is resolved by the application. Overall, the evidence remains insufficient for an independent ACMG/AMP conclusion and requires qualified human review.",
